{
  "dom_id": "step-q251874",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "The formula for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence is ${a}_{n}=5\\cdot {4}^{n}$ for $n\\ge 1.$ What is the recursive formula for this sequence? Express your answer in terms of ${a}_{n}.$\n\n${a}_{n+1}=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,{a}_{1}=$\n{{field-2}}$,\\,n\\ge 1$",
  "worked_solution": "The recursive formula for a geometric sequence is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=r\\cdot {a}_{n}.\n$$\n\nTo complete the formula, we must determine the common ratio $r$ and state the first term ${a}_{1}.$ The first two terms are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =5\\cdot {4}^{1}=5\\cdot 4=20, \\\\ {a}_{2} & =5\\cdot {4}^{2}=5\\cdot 16=80.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{80}{20}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the recursive formula for the geometric sequence is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=4{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=20,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
